WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.029
- So when I said that Mike
Flynn was back in the news

00:00:02.029 --> 00:00:05.480
and his advocating for a military coup

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.780
in the United States was likely protected

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:07.613
by the First Amendment.

00:00:07.613 --> 00:00:08.950
Many people said but wait a minute

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.660
but what about the fact
that he is a former

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:12.620
military officer

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.760
couldn't he be punished
under the Uniform Code

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.190
of Military Justice?

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:19.820
And the answer is maybe, but
he probably should not be.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:24.590
First of all yes is possible
for retired military officers

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.770
to be punished under the Uniform
Code of Military Justice.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:31.190
But it's unlikely that those
laws are going to withstand

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.450
First Amendment scrutiny.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.740
It's actually an issue that
is currently on appeal.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.210
Law professor Steve Vladeck
is heading the charge

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:40.290
to try and overturn the
current case law on this

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.830
and they stand a good
chance of succeeding.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:45.420
So this is one of those cases
where under current law,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.580
it might theoretically be possible.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.850
But if that was ever challenged

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:50.840
and went up to the Supreme Court

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.700
there's a good chance of
that might be overruled.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.133
So we will in fact see
this issue in court.

